        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "45ded900-0dd4-5d0a-90ff-c37d7841294c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Eri Muraoka, Hanako Muraoka, Anne Shirley, Matthew Cuthbert, Marilla Cuthbert\n- Works: Hanako to Anne, An no Yurikago Muraoka Hanako no Shogai, Anne of Green Gables\n- Places: Avonlea, Prince Edward Island\n- Topics: Japanese translation, adaptation, plot\n\nFacts:\n- Hanako to Anne is based on the novel An no Yurikago Muraoka Hanako no Shogai by Eri Muraoka.\n- An no Yurikago Muraoka Hanako no Shogai tells the story of Eri Muraoka’s grandmother, Hanako Muraoka.\n- Hanako Muraoka lived from 1893 to 1968 and had the maiden name Annaka.\n- Hanako Muraoka was the first person to translate Anne of Green Gables into Japanese.\n- Anne of Green Gables recounts the adventures of Anne Shirley, an 11-year-old orphan girl.\n- Anne Shirley is mistakenly sent to Matthew Cuthbert and Marilla Cuthbert, a middle-aged brother and sister.\n- Matthew Cuthbert and Marilla Cuthbert had intended to adopt a boy to help on their farm.\n- Anne of Green Gables is set in the fictional town of Avonlea on Prince Edward Island.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
